19:T51a,## Intent

Some things should exist **once**: a configuration object, a connection pool, a logger, a cache. Singleton guarantees a single instance and a global access point to it.

## How it works

Three moves:

1. Make the **constructor private** so nobody can `new` it.
2. Hold the one instance in a **static field**.
3. Expose a **static `getInstance()`** that creates it on first call and returns the same object forever.

```
class Config {
    private static Config instance;
    private Config() { }                         // no 'new' from outside
    static Config getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) instance = new Config();   // lazy
        return instance;
    }
}
```

## Watch the thread

The lazy check above is **not thread-safe**, two threads can both see `null` and create two instances. Real fixes: **double-checked locking** with a `volatile` field, an **eager** `static final` instance, the **holder idiom**, or (in Java) an **enum** singleton.

## Use it sparingly

A Singleton is **global mutable state** in disguise. It hides dependencies (callers reach for it instead of receiving it), makes unit tests order-dependent, and resists substitution. Prefer **dependency injection**, create one instance and pass it in, and reserve the pattern for genuinely single resources.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-creational","activeLesson":"singleton"}],["$","$L18","singleton",{"lesson":{"id":"singleton","patternId":"lld-creational","title":"Singleton","kind":"pattern","difficulty":"Intro","statement":"Guarantee a class has exactly ONE instance and give the whole program a single point of access to it.","companies":["Amazon","Microsoft","Adobe"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"One instance, ever","code":["class Config {","    private static Config instance;","    private Config() { }                 // constructor is private","    static Config getInstance() {","        if (instance == null)","            instance = new Config();      // created once, lazily","        return instance;","    }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":3,"narration":"The constructor is PRIVATE, no other code can write `new Config()`. That's how the class controls its own instantiation.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"s","name":"Config","fields":["- instance: Config  «static»"],"methods":["- Config()","+ getInstance(): Config  «static»"],"x":1,"y":0.4,"tint":"accent"}],"relations":[],"shownClassIds":["s"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["s"]},"vars":[["constructor","private"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":2,"narration":"A single static field holds the one instance, shared across the whole program.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":[],"shownClassIds":["s"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["s"]},"vars":[["instance","static, one copy"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":4,"narration":"The only way in is the static getInstance(), it creates the instance on first call, then hands back that same object every time after.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":[],"shownClassIds":["s"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["s"]},"vars":[["access","getInstance()"]]}]},{"label":"Everyone shares the same object","code":["Config a = Config.getInstance();","Config b = Config.getInstance();","assert a == b;   // the very same object"],"steps":[{"view":"sequence","codeLine":1,"narration":"ModuleA asks for the config the only way it can, getInstance().","sequence":{"actors":[{"id":"a","label":"ModuleA","kind":"object"},{"id":"cfg","label":"Config","tint":"accent"},{"id":"b","label":"ModuleB","kind":"object"}],"messages":[{"id":"m1","from":"a","to":"cfg","label":"getInstance()","kind":"call"},{"id":"m2","from":"cfg","to":"a","label":"config #1","kind":"return"},{"id":"m3","from":"b","to":"cfg","label":"getInstance()","kind":"call"},{"id":"m4","from":"cfg","to":"b","label":"config #1  (same!)","kind":"return"}],"shownCount":1,"activeIndex":0}},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":1,"narration":"First call: the instance doesn't exist yet, so it's created and returned. Call it config #1.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":2,"activeIndex":1},"vars":[["created","config #1"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":2,"narration":"Later, an unrelated ModuleB calls getInstance() too.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":3,"activeIndex":2}},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":3,"narration":"It gets back the EXACT same config #1, not a new one. a == b. One instance, shared everywhere. That's the Singleton guarantee.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":4,"activeIndex":3},"vars":[["a == b","true ✓"],["instances","1"]]}]}]}}]]}]
